<% @settings_profile_url = settings_org_profile_url(@organization)%>
Hello there!

We notice that <%= @display_login %> is currently under the Standard Terms of Service. As an account using the GitHub Enterprise plan, we kindly ask you to review and accept the GitHub Customer Agreement.

To accept the GitHub Customer Agreement:

1. Navigate to your organization's Settings. Under General, scroll to the "Terms of Service" section.
2. Click "Read the GitHub Customer Agreement".
3. After you've read the GitHub Customer Agreement, click "Sign GitHub customer terms".
4. In the text field, enter the name of the company, non-profit, or group that owns the organization account. This is the entity that will enter into an agreement with GitHub.
5. To agree to the GitHub Customer Agreement on behalf of your entity, click "Accept terms".

We appreciate your prompt attention to this matter.

Review GitHub customer terms: <%= @settings_profile_url %>

Note: If you get a 404 page, make sure you’re signed in as an owner of <%= @display_login %>.

You're receiving this email because you're an owner of the <%= @display_login %> organization on GitHub.
